  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...\nIssued 302 AM MDT SUN AUG 30 2026\nModel guidance continues to show solid consensus for a long-\nwave trough and closed low pressure system to stall near the \nOregon and Washington coastline through the extended period. \nThis setup keeps the forecast area under persistent, cool \nsouthwesterly flow aloft.\n\nAs shortwave energy rotates around the parent low, shower and \nthunderstorm chances will increase Wednesday into Thursday, \nparticularly over southeast Oregon and the West-Central Idaho \nMountains. SW Idaho valley locations may see less widespread \nprecipitation due to dry slotting between the main circulation \nand monsoonal moisture to the east, but cooler temperatures will\nbe felt region-wide.\n\nTemperatures drop significantly starting Thursday, falling back\nto 5 to 10 degrees below normal with valley highs held in the\n70s through the weekend. Afternoon gusty winds will remain a\nprimary feature through late week, particularly across higher\nterrain and open valleys of southeast Oregon. Uncertainty\nremains regarding exact shower timing into Friday and Saturday\nas minor individual impulses traverse the flow, but overall\nconfidence is high for a cooler and more unsettled pattern\nheading into next weekend.",
